  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "kind": "prep",
      "primary_message": "Drain and finely mince the capers. Finely mince the cornichons. Mince the garlic. Mince the fresh parsley leaves. Pick the mint leaves from the stems and mince them. Mince the anchovy fillets. Mince the shallot. Thinly slice the leftover grilled and keep it cold until you use it. Thinly slice the red onion.",
      "secondary_message": "2 tbsp capers\n8 cornichons\n2 medium cloves garlic\n1 cup fresh parsley leaves, plus more for garnish\n½ cup fresh mint, plus more for garnish\n6 anchovy fillets\n1 small shallot\n0.34 kg leftover grilled\n1 red onion"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "For the Salsa Verde: Combine capers, cornichons, garlic, parsley, mint, anchovies, shallot, mustard, and sherry vinegar in a large bowl. Whisking constantly, drizzle in extra-virgin olive oil. Season to taste with salt and pepper and set aside.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "For the Salad: Shuck and grill corn over a hot grill or under the broiler, turning frequently, until tender and charred in spots, about 8 minutes total. Alternatively, place corn on a microwave-safe plate and microwave until steamed and tender, about 7 minutes. Allow to rest until cool enough to handle, then cut off kernels. Discard cobs.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "Combine corn, steak, and red onion in a large bowl. Add 1/2 cup of the salsa verde and toss to combine. Season to taste with salt and pepper. Transfer to a serving platter and spoon additional salsa verde over. Garnish with parsley and mint leaves and serve immediately. Extra salsa verde can be stored in a sealed container in the refrigerator for up to 1 week.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
